 figure out what  this brain does normally when the first  brain is still working but they have  seen that if the first brain is  destroyed this second brain can take  over to some limited capacity they saw  it firsthand when a team of scp  foundation agents lured an  scp-1788-1 instance into a kill zone and  an mtf sniper blew open its head but  despite its brain and most of its  sensory function being utterly destroyed  the monster kept going and was able to  subdue other agents before being brought  down another main difference in the  overall anatomy of an  scp-1788-1 instance from a normal human  is its arms more specifically that it  has extra arms a second pair of arms sit  just below the regular main arms  extending out of the armpits they're  much smaller but they're just as strong  and flexible and testing has shown that  scp-1788-1 instances can use all four  arms at the same time if they need to  but to maintain their cover most of the  time instances just hold the second arms  folded up and close to their sides where  nobody can tell they're there from the  instance's massive size when an instance  is wearing clothes and has their arms  folded up it's almost impossible to tell  which is an  scp-1788-1 instance and which is just a  normal if obese human being as you can  see  scp-1788 causes quite a few drastic  changes to the human body in fact you  can probably say that these creatures  aren't even properly human anymore but  despite all these changes  scp-1788-1 instances are as you can also  see really hard to differentiate from  regular humans the perfect stealth  predator right but what exactly do  instances do with all these additional  abilities and modifications well like we  said the second part of  scp-1788 changes the behavior of the  people it infects namely they become  predatory the behavior of  scp-1788 instances was hard to observe  since finding them at all was such a  difficult task but eventually the  research team located a large gro