e  observed in the same city they kept a  strict ratio of one  scp-1788-1 instance for every 100 000  humans the same behavior apex predators  like bears and sharks practice this  behavior of avoiding each other happens  for almost the entire calendar year at  first the foundation thought this  avoiding practice never stopped but  about a year into the surveillance  program something seemed to change  several of the tagged  scp-1788-1 instances in the city  actively began to gravitate toward each  other's territories the foundation  prepared for the inevitably brutal  fights but something even stranger  happened they met each other and didn't  fight in fact they went into each  other's homes the recon teams reported  that the  scp-1788-1 instances were in fact mating  with one another apparently an annual  mating season causes this change in  behavior the  scp-1788-1 mated and then left each  other as quickly as they'd met needless  to say  scp-1788-1 instances are horrifying apex  predators the foundation's research and  observation teams have gleaned quite a  bit about their anatomy and behavior  respectively but many of the personnel  still hold the burning question why  why do  scp-1788-1 instances hunt what's the  motivation well their uncooperativeness  with interviews makes finding out any  details into their thought process  virtually impossible however there was  one occurrence where one of the captured  instances accidentally let something  slip one of the site directors was  attempting to interrogate an instance  using an electroshock collar at first  the instance brushed off his questions  saying the name on his id was his child  name and when asked by the director what  it wanted from regular people it gave a  simple sneering response grow up or die  now go check out scp-5094 miss j's whiz  kid schoolhouse and scp-053 young girl  for more kid-related anomalies from scp  explained

